  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Protective and Productive Safety Nets for Sustainable Food Systems Transformation: Scale-up the Climate-Friendly Home-Grown School Meals Programme in Kenya</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kenya is aiming to reach 10 million children by 2030 through the scale-up of the school meals programme. This safety net is critical for children in arid and semi-arid land counties, regularly hit by climate shocks. Leveraging on the expertise of the Rome Based Agencies, the JP will support the scale-up of the climate-friendly home-grown school meals programme, in line with the National School Meals Coalition and Kenya?s pathways for food systems transformation.</narrative>
  </description>
